So after applying migrations + seeding admin, I still need the connection string for the app to run. Let me handle that: ask for the pooler connection string. But before asking, maybe I can find the region. Hmm, again I can't get the password.

Wait — maybe I don't need to ask this time: I could ask them to paste it; that's the same blocker. That's unavoidable because the app connects over Postgres with a password. The publishable key is for the Data API only.

Alternatively, I could restructure the app to use the Supabase Data API with the publishable key... not appropriate (would require rewriting Drizzle data access + RLS policies + auth). I'll explain clearly and request the DB password/connection string.

So plan: apply both migrations now (that's real progress and directly what "integrate on this new project" means for the schema), seed the admin user, verify, update .env (project ref + publishable key + URL as documented, DATABASE_URL pending), update docs, then ask for the connection string.

Important: to apply the baseline migration I reuse the exact SQL I used before. Let me apply both.

Also note: previous project still has the schema — the user said forget it. I'll offer (not do) cleanup of the old project.

Also: should I add RLS to the new project's tables? Yes, same as before — consistent posture, and I'll explain.

Let me apply baseline migration now. I'll reuse the same SQL text (it worked). I must be careful to include everything.

Then pitch_deck_workflow.

Then seed admin + test accounts via execute_sql.

